    "title": "Johnson takes readers on a gritty, insane ride through Appalachia in new novel",
    "text": "Johnson takes readers on a gritty, insane ride through Appalachia in new novel\n“Bloodline” by Lee Clay Johnson is the strange love child of “Demon Copperhead” and “Wise Blood,” with a fair amount of Appalachian McCarthy thrown into the mix. It’s Southern Gothic, even if it’s not immediately obvious. It’s gritty and insane, and it’s a clear reflection of the times we’re living in, seen through muddy eyes.\nWinston Alcorn, who presents as a strange mix of Hazel Motes and Donald Trump, is a good, ol’ fashioned, cut-throat shyster. The only person he truly cares about is himself. He takes and takes with no remorse, perpetually preaching his gospel of greed to anyone who will listen and gaining a cult-like following in small-town Tennessee through his wildly successful auctions and illegally broadcast radio show. Winston has “already done everything a man needs to do: sacrifice quietly and alone and secretly hold it against everyone around him.”",
